NAME
     telinit - change runlevel

SYNOPSIS
     telinit RUNLEVEL
     telinit q

DESCRIPTION
     telinit tells init to change to RUNLEVEL (0 to 6), which runs the
     stop scripts of the old level and the start scripts of the new one.
     `telinit q' makes init read /etc/inittab again.

SEE ALSO
     init(8), service(8), shutdown(8)
